### 1. Stop Swallowing HDFS Exceptions (NC-7)
Because syncToDataLake is currently marked as @Async, when it throws a database error, the main thread never hears about it, so it never queues the data for retry.
**File:** HdfsSyncService.java
Locate your syncToDataLake method. Remove @Async and remove the try-catch block that swallows the error:
**Replace with:**
```java
    // CRITICAL FIX: Removed @Async. The caller is already on a background thread.
    // Letting this run synchronously allows the caller to catch exceptions and queue for retry.
    public void syncToDataLake(List<HdfsSyncDto> data) {
        if (data == null || data.isEmpty()) return;
        
        log.info("HDFS_SYNC_START | Target: Hive Data Lake | RecordCount: {}", data.size());
        long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

        try {
            String sql = "UPDATE GL_BALANCE_HDFS SET BALANCE = ?, INR_BALANCE = ? " +
                    "WHERE BRANCH_CODE = ? AND CURRENCY = ? AND CGL = ? AND BALANCE_DATE = ?";

            hiveJdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(sql, new BatchPreparedStatementSetter() {
                @Override
                public void setValues(PreparedStatement ps, int i) throws SQLException {
                    HdfsSyncDto dto = data.get(i);
                    ps.setBigDecimal(1, dto.getNewBalance());
                    ps.setBigDecimal(2, dto.getNewInrBalance());
                    ps.setString(3, dto.getBranch());
                    ps.setString(4, dto.getCurrency());
                    ps.setString(5, dto.getCgl());
                    ps.setDate(6, java.sql.Date.valueOf(dto.getBalanceDate()));
                }

                @Override
                public int getBatchSize() {
                    return data.size();
                }
            });

            log.info("HDFS_SYNC_SUCCESS | Duration: {}ms | Records: {}",
                    (System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime), data.size());

        } catch (DataAccessException e) {
            log.error("HDFS_SYNC_DB_FAIL | Status: Connectivity or Syntax error | Type: {}", e.getClass().getSimpleName());
            // CRITICAL FIX: DO NOT SWALLOW IT. Throw it so JournalRequestServiceImpl queues it!
            throw e; 
        }
    }

```
### 2. Fix the Dead Retry Service & Redis Lock (H-2 & NM-8)
We need to fix the bug where the Redis lock deletes someone else's lock, and extend the lock TTL from 4 minutes to 10 minutes so pods don't overlap.
**File:** HdfsRecoveryService.java
Replace your entire retryFailedHdfsSyncs method:
```java
    @Scheduled(fixedDelay = 300000)
    public void retryFailedHdfsSyncs() {
        String lockKey = "SYSTEM_LOCK_HDFS_RECOVERY";
        boolean lockAcquired = false;

        try {
            // CRITICAL FIX: Lock TTL extended to 10 mins to prevent race conditions under load
            Boolean acquired = stringRedisTemplate.opsForValue()
                .setIfAbsent(lockKey, "LOCKED", 10, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.MINUTES);
            lockAcquired = Boolean.TRUE.equals(acquired);

            if (!lockAcquired) {
                log.debug("HDFS_RECOVERY_SKIPPED | Status: Another node is currently processing.");
                return;
            }

            String fetchSql = "SELECT BATCH_ID FROM HDFS_SYNC_RETRY_QUEUE WHERE STATUS = 'PENDING' AND RETRY_COUNT < 5";
            List<String> failedBatches;
            try {
                failedBatches = oracleJdbcTemplate.query(fetchSql, (rs, rowNum) -> rs.getString("BATCH_ID"));
            } catch (DataAccessException e) {
                log.error("HDFS_RECOVERY_QUERY_FAIL | Error: {}", e.getMessage());
                return;
            }

            if (failedBatches.isEmpty()) return;

            log.info("HDFS RECOVERY: Found {} failed batches.", failedBatches.size());
            for (String batchId : failedBatches) {
                try {
                    processRetry(batchId);
                } catch (DataAccessException | CustomExceptions.DatabaseOperationException e) {
                    log.error("HDFS_RECOVERY_ERROR | Batch: {} | Error: {}", batchId, e.getMessage());
                    incrementRetryCount(batchId);
                }
            }
        } catch (org.springframework.data.redis.RedisConnectionFailureException e) {
            log.error("HDFS_RECOVERY_REDIS_FAIL | Cannot acquire distributed lock.");
        } finally {
            // CRITICAL FIX: Only release if THIS thread actually acquired it!
            if (lockAcquired) {
                try { stringRedisTemplate.delete(lockKey); }
                catch (Exception e) { log.warn("HDFS_LOCK_RELEASE_FAIL"); }
            }
        }
    }

```
### 3. Prevent K8s Pod Out-Of-Sync Errors (NH-6)
Your application is currently using an in-memory cache for permissions. In Kubernetes, this means Pod A won't know about permissions updated on Pod B. We must switch this to Redis.
**File:** CacheConfig.java
Replace the entire class to use the Redis-backed CacheManager:
```java
package com.fincore.JournalService.Config; // Update with your actual package

import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.cache.annotation.EnableCaching;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;

@Configuration
@EnableCaching
@Slf4j
public class CacheConfig {

    @Bean
    public org.springframework.cache.CacheManager cacheManager(
            org.springframework.data.redis.connection.RedisConnectionFactory connectionFactory) {

        log.info("CACHE_CONFIG_INIT | Using Redis-backed CacheManager for K8s compatibility");

        org.springframework.data.redis.cache.RedisCacheConfiguration config =
            org.springframework.data.redis.cache.RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
                .entryTtl(java.time.Duration.ofMinutes(30))
                .disableCachingNullValues()
                .serializeValuesWith(
                    org.springframework.data.redis.serializer.RedisSerializationContext.SerializationPair
                        .fromSerializer(new org.springframework.data.redis.serializer.GenericJackson2JsonRedisSerializer()));

        return org.springframework.data.redis.cache.RedisCacheManager.builder(connectionFactory)
                .cacheDefaults(config)
                .withCacheConfiguration("notification_configs",
                    config.entryTtl(java.time.Duration.ofHours(1)))
                .build();
    }
}

```
### 4. Prevent K8s Out-Of-Memory Crashes (NM-7)
If you generate a large Excel error file, Apache POI creates temporary files on the container's disk. If you don't call .dispose(), the pod's disk fills up and Kubernetes will kill the pod.
**File:** JournalBulkValidationService.java
Find the generateErrorExcelFast method and modify the try block:
**Change this:**
```java
    try (SXSSFWorkbook workbook = new SXSSFWorkbook(100)) {
        // ... build workbook ...
        ByteArrayOutputStream out = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
        workbook.write(out);
        return out.toByteArray();
    }

```
**To this:**
```java
    SXSSFWorkbook workbook = new SXSSFWorkbook(100);
    try {
        // ... build workbook (keep your existing sheet building logic here) ...
        ByteArrayOutputStream out = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
        workbook.write(out);
        return out.toByteArray();
    } finally {
        workbook.dispose();  // CRITICAL FIX: Cleans up temp files on K8s disk
